Q: What is the procedure for escalating a triage queue delay at the Kisumu facility?
A: The threshold is 30 minutes past the allocated triage slot. At that point the staff member logs the case under Queue Escalation, tags the duty nurse practitioner, and notes the patient's status in the log. The escalation board is reviewed every 15 minutes, so a properly logged case is picked up quickly. As with every workflow, clinical decisions stay with the AfyaPlus clinical team.
