Q: How long do lab results take, and what does 'Pending review' mean?
A: Standard laboratory results are released to the Results tab within 48 hours of sample collection. If a patient sees Pending review, that means a clinician is handling the release personally and will contact them, so no action is needed from the front desk beyond confirming the contact number is current. As with every workflow, clinical decisions stay with an AfyaPlus provider.
