Q: The dispensary has run out of an item on a patient's prescription. What do we tell the patient?
A: Staff open the item under Dispensary and log a stock query, which notifies the county supply coordinator automatically. The expected restock date on the item card is the information to share with the patient. Any change to what was prescribed is for the prescriber to decide, not dispensary or front-desk staff. As with every workflow, clinical decisions stay with the AfyaPlus clinical team.
